# Purpose

This document defines the frontend engineering standards for the hubIO platform.

Its purpose is to ensure every frontend feature is maintainable, scalable, predictable, and aligned with the platform architecture while providing a consistent user experience across all products.

---

# Scope

This standard defines:

* Frontend engineering principles
* Presentation architecture
* Responsibility boundaries
* Interface consistency
* State ownership philosophy
* Frontend scalability
* Frontend governance

It intentionally excludes implementation details, framework-specific guidance, component implementation, and styling conventions, which are defined by their respective Engineering Standards.

---

# Constitutional Interpretation

This document extends the hubIO Engineering Constitution.

It applies constitutional engineering principles to frontend development, ensuring the user interface remains maintainable, scalable, and capable of supporting long-term product evolution without unnecessary technical complexity.

